  ["LJz"] = "It tightens around your wrist as you take it on.",
  ["LK"] = "This is no funhouse. Leave the miners and their drilling-worms alone and get out! We have already enough trouble without you.",
  ["LK0"] = "Do you wish to become a jester and join the fools guild?",
  ["LK1"] = "I'm sure it suits you well.",
  ["LK2"] = "No, you aren't! Why do only fools apply for the fools guild?",
  ["LK3"] = "Eeeek! What have you done?? These pies are crawling with bugs! Those must be the infamous parcel bugs! Get some new pies at once you wannabe fool, and this time without any bugs!",
  ["LK4"] = "No, you don't! Why do only fools apply for the fools guild?",
  ["LK5"] = "Too bad, I'm convinced you have it in you.",
  ["LK6"] = "You won't be successful in the fool's world with such an attitude.",
  ["LK7"] = "You wasted the disguise?? Why do only fools apply for the fools guild? Here... try again, but be wittier this time.",
  ["LK8"] = "npc.bozo.mission_20_t1_1 \\z\n\tnpc.bozo.mission_20_t1_2",
  ["LK9"] = "npc.bozo.mission_21_t1 \\z\n\tnpc.bozo.mission_21_t2 \\z\n\tnpc.bozo.mission_21_t3",
  ["LKA"] = "Huhu, please don't hurt me with your {}! Reason of your visit?",
  ["LKB"] = "I was a {}, too, before I died!! What do you want from me?",
  ["LKC"] = "{}, is that right?! What do you want from me?",
  ["LKD"] = "From now on, you shall be known as |PLAYERNAME|, the wolf girl. You shall be fast and smart as Morgrar, the great white wolf. He shall guide your path.",
  ["LKE"] = "From now on, you shall be known as |PLAYERNAME|, the bear warrior. You shall be strong and proud as Angros, the great dark bear. He shall guide your path.",
  ["LKF"] = "Great riddle, isn't it? If you can tell me the correct answer, I will give you something. Hehehe!",
  ["LKG"] = "My surreal numbers are based on astonishing facts. Are you interested in learning the secret of mathemagics?",
  ["LKH"] = "<munch>",
  ["LKI"] = "",
  ["LKJ"] = "Hello, hello, |PLAYERNAME|! Please come in, look, and buy! I'm a specialist for all sorts of {tools}. Just ask me for a {trade} to see my offers! You can also ask me for general {hints} about the game. ...",
  ["LKK"] = "You can also ask me about each {citizen} of the isle.",
  ["LKL"] = "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at {}.",
  ["LKM"] = "ok.",
  ["LKN"] = "So you ask me for a {{}} to begin your adventure?",
  ["LKO"] = "What? I have already gave you one {{}}!",
  ["LKP"] = "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at {}.",
  ["LKQ"] = "So receive the protection of the twist of fate, pilgrim.",
  ["LKR"] = "This is a special blessing I can bestow upon you once you have obtained at least one of the other blessings and which functions a bit differently. ... \\z\n\tIt only works when you're killed by other adventurers, which means that at least half of the damage leading to your death was caused by others, not by monsters or the environment. ... \\z\n\tThe {twist of fate} will not reduce the death penalty like the other blessings, but instead prevent you from losing your other blessings as well as the amulet of loss, should you wear one. It costs the same as the other blessings. ... \\z\n\tWould you like to receive that protection for a sacrifice of |PVPBLESSCOST| gold, child?",
  ["LKS"] = "Some call us nature spirits or peri but we prefer the term fae. Most of us are rather reclusive and live peaceful lives in our secret realm. We only leave it in order to protect our home. ... \\z\n\tWe tend to be secretive about our true nature, but I guess there was once an elven sage who visited our realm and put his experiences down on paper. There might be a book about the fae in the library of Ab'Dendriel.",
  ["LKT"] = "So receive the protection of the twist of fate, pilgrim.",
  ["LKU"] = "This is a special blessing I can bestow upon you once you have obtained at least one of the other blessings and which functions a bit differently. ... \\z\n\tIt only works when you're killed by other adventurers, which means that at least half of the damage leading to your death was caused by others, not by monsters or the environment. ... \\z\n\tThe {twist of fate} will not reduce the death penalty like the other blessings, but instead prevent you from losing your other blessings as well as the amulet of loss, should you wear one. It costs the same as the other blessings. ... \\z\n\tWould you like to receive that protection for a sacrifice of |PVPBLESSCOST| gold, child?",
  ["LKV"] = "Good, just take this spectral essence and use it on the strange carving in this building as well as on the corresponding tile in our base at Northport ...",
  ["LKW"] = "As soon as you have charged the portal tiles that way, report about the spectral portals.",
  ["LKX"] = "...if the expected constant is higher than... Hmmm, who are you?? What do you want?",
  ["LKY"] = "...then I could transform a spell to bend... How can anyone expect me to work under these conditions?? What do you want?",
  ["LKZ"] = "...if my calculations are correct, I will be able to revive... Arrgghh!! What do you want?",
  ["LKa"] = "You need some kind of pure elemental soil from the {} Overlord. Come back when you've got it.",
  ["LKb"] = "So you ask me for a {{}} to begin your adventure?",
  ["LKc"] = "What? I have already gave you one {{}}!",
  ["LKd"] = "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at {}.",
  ["LKe"] = "So receive the protection of the twist of fate, pilgrim.",
  ["LKf"] = "This is a special blessing I can bestow upon you once you have obtained at least one of the other blessings and which functions a bit differently. ... \\z\n\tIt only works when you're killed by other adventurers, which means that at least half of the damage leading to your death was caused by others, not by monsters or the environment. ... \\z\n\tThe {twist of fate} will not reduce the death penalty like the other blessings, but instead prevent you from losing your other blessings as well as the amulet of loss, should you wear one. It costs the same as the other blessings. ... \\z\n\tWould you like to receive that protection for a sacrifice of |PVPBLESSCOST| gold, child?",
  ["LKg"] = "I sell a selection of {}",
  ["LKh"] = "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at {}.",
  ["LKi"] = "Oh my! You look so great in your uniform! You archpostwomen are not only daring but also beautiful. Here take it, that's the key you wanted. Just promise to visit me now and then!",
  ["LKj"] = "Great! That's the word of a true fool! Maybe you want to write the names down. Here we go: Deliver a cookie to: ...",
  ["LKk"] = "The pompous hero Avar Tar in Edron, Simon the greedy beggar on Fibula, the pirate Ariella on the Shattered Isles, the dubious Lorbas next to the ruins of the Dark Cathedral, King Markwin in the underground city Mintwalin ...",
  ["LKl"] = "The shaman Hjaern on the ice island Nibelor, the witch Wyda in the Green Claw Swamp, the ape Hairycles in the jungle city Banuta ...",
  ["LKm"] = "The orc king in the orc fortress Uldrek's Rock and the last one to EITHER Yaman, the green djinn, OR, Nah'Bob, the blue djinn ...",
  ["LKn"] = "A piece of cake isn't it? Did you take notes? If you need the list again, just ask me for it. Otherwise leave now and report about the mission whenever you're done.",
  ["LKo"] = "You shaved the emperor, but lost the beard? What kind of fool are you? Well, at least he will have a nice surprise when he wakes up ...",
  ["LKp"] = "Are you sure you want to waste a part of your limited lifetime on a quest that makes a fool of yourself and which might award you with the prestigious title of a grand fool in a far away future?",
  ["LKq"] = "Still, as a small recognition of your accomplishments I'm willing to tell you how to get your own jester outfit. If you are interested in more fun and adventures, ask me for more missions.",
  ["LKr"] = "What a foolish decision! You are indeed a worthy candidate! But let's talk about business ...",
  ["LKs"] = "Being a jester is not just about telling jokes. A good jester heavily relies on requisites ...",
  ["LKt"] = "Getting some requisites will be your first job. First of all we need a good supply of water squirt flowers ...",
  ["LKu"] = "I'm making them on my own in my spare time but I need the right material. South of Thais, next to the Whiteflower Temple, you will find the ideal flowers ...",
  ["LKv"] = "Take a kitchen knife, cut the thickest and healthiest flower and bring it here. Then talk to me about your mission.",
  ["LKw"] = "So you want to make a total fool of yourself? Fine with me, but note that becoming a real fool means more than being just an ordinary fool ...",
  ["LKx"] = "You will have to master a whole series of challenging, lengthy and, above all, totally foolish quests ...",
  ["LKy"] = "Wow, your stupidity would be pride and joy for every fool. You've already applied as a member. Let's rather talk about your current mission.",
  ["LKz"] = "Oh boy, why do only fools apply for the fools guild?",
  ["LL"] = "We understand the ways of the earth like nobody else.",
  ["LL0"] = "Get out o' here!*HICKS*",
  ["LL1"] = "Get out o' here!*HICKS*",
  ["LL2"] = "Get out o' here!*HICKS*",
  ["LL3"] = "Precisely {}, young one.",
  ["LL4"] = "Well, well, a new {}! Want me to bring you somewhere nice? Just say {yes}.",
  ["LL5"] = "{} What do you say, {yes} or {no}?",
  ["LL6"] = "By tempest! What's all this gold weighing us down? Don't you think that's a little risky with all \\z these pirates around? You can take {} with you, but that's it. Drop the rest or {donate} it to the \\z Adventurers' Orphans Fund, really.",
  ["LL7"] = "Changed your mind? Which city do you want to head to, {}?",
  ["LL8"] = "Changed your mind? Which city do you want to head to, {}?",
  ["LL9"] = "I recommend you travel there as soon as possible.",
