  ["xz"] = "Oh, I'm sorry. I'm not buying less than 5 blueberries.",
  ["y0"] = "Ah, what a pretty ribbon. Reminds me of the elusive dragonlings - they're quite elegant and vain. They would probably welcome a decorative element. They're sometimes spotted during volcano eruptions.",
  ["y1"] = "What a neat little elvish gadget. Did you know a diapason works with vibrations to create sound? I actually think this could work on a creature made of crystals.",
  ["y2"] = "I'm against violence towards any creature. I've heard those barbarians in the desert use it for disobedient dromedaries.",
  ["y3"] = "Oh, what a nice little plant! Did you know it's supposed to bring luck? So is the lady bug. Both of them might actually go well together.",
  ["y4"] = "I've heard that there once was a gang of manta ray riders who liked to adorn their mantas with a foxtail. Don't ask me why, maybe they like how it floats in the wind when running really fast?",
  ["y5"] = "What a strange device! This looks like a tool for someone who creates golems and modifies living creatures. You could probably tame a modded creature with it, but I doubt they live in the wild.",
  ["y6"] = "Oh, that's one of the favourite foods of a crustacea gigantica. I think you can just distract it with the food and quickly jump on its back.",
  ["y7"] = "Have you ever encountered a magma crawler? They only eat and drink really hot things. You could probably try and make one drink some glow wine - and quickly mount it as long as it's drunk.",
  ["y8"] = "Hm. What an interesting find. This is definitely not used for any sort of animal. Maybe a vehicle? I can imagine it could be used for a bike of some sorts.",
  ["y9"] = "Some call me {animal} whisperer. Others say I'm just crazy. I refer to myself as a simple {stable} keeper.",
  ["yD"] = "Oh. In that case, maybe you're interested in a {trade} - I sell potions and buy a few other things.",
  ["yK"] = "Oh. Well, if you change your mind, let me know.",
  ["yL"] = "No, you haven't. If you're looking for the way to Hyacinth, just leave the village to the north and then go east. I've marked it on your map!",
